Plan for the containers:
I will have two separate containers, one for Postgres and one for the Node.js back-end.  The front-end will be deployed by itself, communicate with the back-end container, which will pull data from the Postgres container.  Most resources suggest using docker compose and have a docker-compose.yml for orchestrating communication between the two.  I will be making this bridge from scratch.
